# Phase XX – Release Readiness & Component Refresh Metadata Enhancements

## Objective

Improve the Deployment Readiness page, Component Refresh metadata handling, and overall UI consistency by ensuring that deployment data is always loaded correctly from the database, refresh operations behave consistently, and users can clearly identify when the component information was last refreshed.

---

# Enhancement 1 – Deployment Readiness should load existing DB data

## Problem

Currently, when the Deployment Refresh job completes successfully, backend logs show that records are updated into H2 database.

However, returning to the Deployment Readiness page does not display those records.

This results in users assuming refresh has failed even though database contains valid data.

---

## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-1.1

When a user selects an Environment/Namespace,

the application shall first read Deployment Readiness information from H2 database.

No Kubernetes API call should be triggered automatically.

---

### AC-1.2

If deployment data exists in database,

UI shall immediately display stored deployment information.

---

### AC-1.3

If no deployment data exists,

UI shall display an appropriate empty state.

Example:

> No deployment readiness information available.
> Click "Refresh Deployment Status" to retrieve latest deployment information.

---

### AC-1.4

Database becomes the primary source for Deployment Readiness page.

Kubernetes should never be queried simply because the user selected an environment.

---

### AC-1.5

Deployment Refresh button is the only action that should refresh deployment information from Kubernetes.

---

# Enhancement 2 – Refresh Deployment Status behaviour

## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-2.1

Clicking **Refresh Deployment Status**

shall:

- Create background Job
- Call Kubernetes
- Recalculate deployment readiness
- Update Deployment tables
- Update validation status
- Update validation messages
- Persist everything into database

---

### AC-2.2

Immediately after refresh completes,

UI should automatically reload latest Deployment data from DB.

User should not need to leave and reopen page.

---

### AC-2.3

If refresh is still running,

show message similar to:

> Deployment validation is running in background.
> Latest deployment information will appear automatically after completion.

---

### AC-2.4

Backend should not require browser refresh.

Automatic reload should occur after job completion.

---

# Enhancement 3 – Validation Status Tooltip

Currently Validation Status and Validation Message are shown separately.

This wastes screen space.

---

## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-3.1

Validation Status column remains visible.

Example:

- Passed
- Warning
- Failed

---

### AC-3.2

Validation Message should appear as Tooltip.

Hovering Validation Status shall display complete validation message.

---

### AC-3.3

Tooltip should support multi-line content.

---

### AC-3.4

Validation Message column may be removed if tooltip fully replaces it.

