# Enhancement 4 – Component Refresh Metadata Table

Introduce metadata table to track last successful Component Refresh.

---

## New Table

```
component_refresh_metadata
```

---

### Suggested Columns

| Column | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| id | Primary Key |
| team_key | Team identifier |
| fix_version | Fix Version |
| refreshed_at | Last refresh timestamp |
| refreshed_by | Username |
| created_at | Timestamp |
| updated_at | Timestamp |

---

## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-4.1

Whenever Generate Report stores updated Components,

system shall also update

component_refresh_metadata.

---

### AC-4.2

Metadata record shall be uniquely maintained using

- Team Key
- Fix Version

---

### AC-4.3

Repeated Generate Report operations shall update

refreshed_at

instead of creating duplicate rows.

---

### AC-4.4

Latest timestamp always represents the most recent successful Component Refresh.

---

# Enhancement 5 – Update Metadata during Generate Report

Current Generate Report flow:

Load Components

↓

User Overrides

↓

Generate Report

↓

Update Components

---

## Updated Flow

Load Components

↓

Store Components

↓

Preview

↓

User Overrides

↓

Generate Report

↓

Update Components

↓

Update Component Refresh Metadata

↓

Start Report Generation

---

## Acceptance Criteria

Metadata update must happen immediately before actual Report Generation starts.

---

# Enhancement 6 – Show Last Component Refresh Timestamp

Users should always know how fresh component information is.

---

## Display Location

Display Last Component Refresh on:

- Generate Report
- Review Commits
- Release Readiness
- Scan History

Do NOT display on:

- Dashboard
- Settings

---

## UI Location

Top-right section.

Immediately below blue header.

Within white content area.

Consistent across all four pages.

---

## Display Format

Example

```
Last Component Refresh

IST
28-Jul-2026 10:42:15 AM

CST
27-Jul-2026 11:12:15 PM
```

---

### Acceptance Criteria

### AC-6.1

Timestamp shall be loaded from

component_refresh_metadata.

---

### AC-6.2

Timestamp displayed using

- IST
- CST

---

### AC-6.3

Display must include

- Date
- Time
- AM/PM

---

### AC-6.4

Timestamp updates automatically after Generate Report refreshes Components.

---

### AC-6.5

Timestamp should never be calculated on client.

Backend provides formatted values.

---

# Enhancement 7 – UI Consistency

Timestamp widget should look identical across

- Generate Report
- Review Commits
- Release Readiness
- Scan History

---

### Acceptance Criteria

- Same font
- Same spacing
- Same alignment
- Same colors
- Same formatting
- Responsive layout

---

# Backend Requirements

- Read deployment data from DB by default.
- Refresh Deployment updates DB.
- UI reloads from DB.
- Metadata table maintained.
- Timestamp API exposed.
- Timestamp reused by all pages.
- Avoid unnecessary Kubernetes calls.
- Follow existing asynchronous Job architecture.
- Maintain existing functionality.

---

# Logging Requirements

Add INFO logs for:

- Deployment Refresh Started
- Deployment Refresh Completed
- Deployment Data Loaded from DB
- Component Metadata Updated
- Timestamp Retrieved
- Timestamp Display Request

Add DEBUG logs for:

- Metadata SQL operations
- Deployment reload
- Timestamp formatting
- Job completion

---

# Definition of Done (DoD)

The enhancement is complete only if all of the following are satisfied:

- [ ] Deployment page loads existing deployment data directly from H2 database.
- [ ] Selecting an environment does not trigger Kubernetes calls.
- [ ] Refresh Deployment Status refreshes Kubernetes data and persists latest records.
- [ ] UI automatically reloads refreshed deployment data after background job completion.
- [ ] Validation Status displays tooltip with detailed validation message.
- [ ] New `component_refresh_metadata` table created.
- [ ] Metadata updated after every successful Generate Report component refresh.
- [ ] Metadata uniquely maintained by Team Key + Fix Version.
- [ ] Last Component Refresh timestamp displayed on Generate Report page.
- [ ] Last Component Refresh timestamp displayed on Review Commits page.
- [ ] Last Component Refresh timestamp displayed on Release Readiness page.
- [ ] Last Component Refresh timestamp displayed on Scan History page.
- [ ] Timestamp shown in both IST and CST with AM/PM.
- [ ] Dashboard and Settings do not display the timestamp.
- [ ] Logging implemented using INFO and DEBUG best practices.
- [ ] Existing Generate Report functionality remains unchanged.
- [ ] Existing Deployment Readiness functionality remains intact.
- [ ] No regression introduced.
- [ ] Code passes compilation and regression testing.
- [ ] UI verified for responsive layout and consistent design.
